Diagnostic: env-gated stylesheet-invalidation logging (WEBKIT_STYLE_LOG=1).

Device gdb sampling of a franceinfo load shows ~44% of main-thread time in
CSS style resolution (TreeResolver/applyMatchedProperties/styleForPseudoElement).
Hypothesis: the site's ~42 stylesheets complete loading out of DOM order, and
each out-of-order completion inserts a sheet before an already-active one, which
analyzeStyleSheetChange classifies as Reset/Reconstruct -> full resolver rebuild
+ (often) invalidateAllStyle full-document restyle, repeated many times per load.

This counts and classifies the events to confirm the lever before optimizing.
With WEBKIT_STYLE_LOG=1 (off by default, zero overhead when unset) the WebProcess
logs on stderr, per Scope::updateActiveStyleSheets:
  [stylelog] updateActiveStyleSheets doc=.. updateType=.. resolver=Reconstruct|Reset|Additive
             oldSheets=.. newSheets=.. added=.. body=.. missingStyle=..
  [stylelog]   -> invalidateAllStyle (reconstruct=.. invalidateAll=..)   | -> targeted invalidate added=..
Aggregate the resolver= and invalidateAllStyle counts across one load to see how
many full rebuilds/restyles the sheet-arrival cadence actually causes.

